# A read off a view of any kind may bear a NaN of any bits, so what is reckoned from it is made a clean NaN in front of whoever does not take such a one: a store by the kind of the cell is such a user.
# In the turns laid out for Int32Array the read is a whole number: no NaN. Marked all the same, its sum was made clean in front of the store, and the machine no longer saw that a whole number is read, raised and stored:
# a thousand elements: Int32 2,209 > 10,210 instructions, Int16 4,220 > 11,220, plain Bun 8,070 and 4,592. Where the kind found in front holds no floats, or the type lists none, the read is neither settled nor marked.
# Four turns of a load-and-add and a store: eight operations.
# f1 = go
# REQUIRES(TURNS): x86_64
# RUN(TURNS): loops f1:Body mechanisms=all
# TURNS: loop: operations 9, patches 0
# arm64 has no operation that loads and adds or stores what it reckons: the same four turns and the jump are seventeen operations there, as those of three more kinds are on both machines: five loops of seventeen.
# REQUIRES(ARM): arm64
# RUN(ARM): loops f1:Body mechanisms=all
# ARM-COUNT-5: loop: operations 17, patches 0
# ARM-NOT: loop: operations 17, patches 0
